#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For workflows that require many single-qubit $R_X(\\theta)$ or two-qubit rotations (such as in a variational ansatz or when simulating the time evolution of quantum systems), this constraint causes the circuit depth to grow rapidly. However, fractional gates remove this requirement, because the single- and two-qubit rotations are executed directly, and create a more efficient (and thus error-suppressed) quantum circuit.\n"
"<span id=\"when-not-to-use\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""
"Para flujos de trabajo que requieren muchas rotaciones de un solo qubit $R_X(\\theta)$ o de dos qubits (como en un ansatz variacional o al simular la evolución temporal de sistemas cuánticos), esta restricción hace que la profundidad del circuito crezca rápidamente. Sin embargo, las puertas fraccionarias eliminan este requisito, ya que las rotaciones de uno y dos qubits se ejecutan directamente, creando un circuito cuántico más eficiente (y por tanto con los errores más suprimidos).\n"
"<span id=\"when-not-to-use\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When *not* to use fractional gates {#when-not-to-use-fractional-gates}"
msgstr ""
"Cuándo *no* usar puertas fraccionarias {#when-not-to-use-fractional-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is important to note that fractional gates are an *experimental* feature "
"and the behavior of the `use_fractional_gates` flag may change in the "
"future. Look to the [release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/release-notes) for new versions of Qiskit Runtime for more "
"information. See also the API reference documentation for "
"[QiskitRuntimeService.backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backend), which describes "
"`use_fractional_gates`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Es importante tener en cuenta que las puertas fraccionarias son una "
"característica *experimental* y que el comportamiento de la bandera "
"`use_fractional_gates` puede cambiar en el futuro. Consulta las [notas de "
"versión](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/release-notes) "
"para nuevas versiones de Qiskit Runtime para obtener más información. "
"Consulta también la documentación de referencia de la API para "
"[QiskitRuntimeService.backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backend), que describe "
"`use_fractional_gates`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additionally, the Qiskit transpiler has limited capability to use "
"$R_{ZZ}(\\theta)$ in its optimization passes. This requires you to take more"
" care in crafting and optimizing circuits that contain these instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Además, el transpilador de Qiskit tiene capacidad limitada para usar "
"$R_{ZZ}(\\theta)$ en sus pases de optimización. Esto requiere que tengas más"
" cuidado al construir y optimizar circuitos que contengan estas "
"instrucciones.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lastly, using fractional gates is not supported for:\n"
"- [Dynamic circuits](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow)\n"
"- [Pauli twirling](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#pauli-twirling) - however, [measurement twirling with TREX](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex) *is* supported.\n"
"- [Probabilistic error cancellation](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec)\n"
"- [Zero-noise extrapolation (using probabilistic error amplification)](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-amplification-pea)\n"
msgstr ""
"Por último, el uso de puertas fraccionarias no es compatible con:\n"
"- [Circuitos dinámicos](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow)\n"
"- [Pauli twirling](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#pauli-twirling) — sin embargo, el [twirling de medición con TREX](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex) *sí* es compatible.\n"
"- [Cancelación probabilística de errores](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec)\n"
"- [Extrapolación de ruido cero (usando amplificación probabilística de errores)](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-amplification-pea)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Read the guide on [primitive options](/guides/runtime-options-overview) to "
"learn more about customizing the error mitigation and suppression techniques"
